---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Manny Mayorga and the thinking behind Rough at Sea.">
  <section class="about-hero shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / MANNY MAYORGA</p>
      <h1>I like software that explains itself.</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="about-intro">
      <p>I’m a developer in Arizona interested in the seam between systems and interfaces—the place where technical decisions become something a person can feel.</p>
      <p>Rough at Sea is where I document that work honestly: the useful patterns, the wrong turns, and the moment a simpler architecture becomes the better one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-details">
    <div class="shell about-grid">
      <p class="section-number">WORKING PRINCIPLES</p>
      <div class="belief-list">
        <article><span>01</span><h2>Clarity is a technical feature.</h2><p>Names, boundaries, interfaces, and documentation all shape whether a system can be understood and changed safely.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h2>Complexity needs to earn rent.</h2><p>A sophisticated solution is worthwhile only when it creates proportionate value. Deleting infrastructure can be architecture work.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h2>Design belongs in the implementation.</h2><p>Good front-end work connects visual intent to responsive behavior, accessibility, performance, and maintainable code.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section shell">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">NOW</p><h2>Building the ship<br />as I sail it.</h2></div>
    <div class="now-list">
      <p><span>Learning</span> Static architecture, content systems, and expressive interfaces.</p>
      <p><span>Writing</span> Practical notes about decisions rather than victory laps.</p>
      <p><span>Exploring</span> Small tools that make complicated work feel legible.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
